  order_basis: 'Revised 2026-09-05 by the operator: the five CONTROL revisits of 9DTact_hard_3mm_r1
    are dropped, and 9DTact_medium_2mm_r1 is dropped because its gel took 0.27 mm
    of permanent set on 2026-09-04 and its replicate r2 carries that design. 59 entries
    -> 53. Replicates stay non-adjacent so replicate variance still carries mounting
    and day-to-day drift rather than five minutes of the same session.'
  structure: principle outer, probe middle, sensor inner
  structure_decided: '2026-09-05'
  structure_basis: 'Finish every probe on 9DTact''s 17 units before starting DIGIT,
    rather than carrying one probe across all 53. One principle then completes as
    a whole: its analysis can begin while the next is still being collected, a protocol
    fault shows up in a finished dataset instead of a thin slice of everything, and
    the ball4 calibration data that test 2 needs arrives early enough to check the
    reconstruction before the bulk of the campaign is spent.'
