  runs_total: 477
  probe_order_basis: 'cyl4 first: a flat face pins the depth zero four times better
    than a sphere (+-0.003 against +-0.014 mm) and its 4.00 mm imprint is the scale
    reference. ball4 second because it CALIBRATES the shape reconstruction -- a known
    radius pressed to known depths is what the depth-from-intensity lookup is built
    from -- so having it early lets the reconstruction be checked on all nine designs
    before the rest of the campaign is spent. The four held-out shapes and the four
    resolution pairs follow. ball8 is last and carries tests 1 and 4: force estimation
    over the fixed 0-4 N range, then the saturation ramp, which damages gels and so
    must come after everything else. ball4 cannot do test 1 -- inside the thickness
    x 0.9 backstop it reaches only about 2.2 N on a soft 3 mm gel and 0.5 N on a soft
    1 mm one, so the fixed range the comparison needs is out of reach.'
  sensor_order_basis: 'From the ball4 pass on: replicate 1 in full, then replicate
    2, each sorted soft -> medium -> hard and 3 mm -> 2 mm -> 1 mm. The cyl4 pass
    ran in the original interleaved order, which was hard to follow at the bench.'
  sensor_order_from_ball4:
  - 9DTact_soft_3mm_r1
  - 9DTact_soft_2mm_r1
