indenter:
  dataset: 20260904_4mmBall
  tip: ball, 4 mm diameter (2 mm radius)
  mounted: '2026-09-04'
  note: 'recorded because it sets the contact geometry: Hertz contact radius is sqrt(2*R*depth),
    so R halves the radius at a given depth against the 4 mm RADIUS previously assumed
    when estimating mm per pixel. No mm/px calibration exists, so contact sizes stay
    in pixels'
